WEBVTT

00:00:00.437 --> 00:00:05.237
Membership tier is an ordered category, but it can be represented in more than one way.

00:00:05.237 --> 00:00:08.837
An ordinal code preserves the rank from Bronze through Platinum.

00:00:08.837 --> 00:00:13.747
A one-hot representation avoids expressing the category as a single numeric distance.

00:00:13.747 --> 00:00:16.462
Neither changes the underlying business meaning.

00:00:16.462 --> 00:00:22.872
The better representation depends on how the analytical method will interpret the values.

00:00:22.872 --> 00:00:25.667
When reading the example, do not read punctuation one character at a time.

00:00:25.667 --> 00:00:31.312
Start with the purpose of the query, then identify the input rows, the operation being applied,

00:00:31.312 --> 00:00:33.637
and the shape of the expected output.

00:00:33.637 --> 00:00:39.697
In a real setting such as a hospital combining patient tables, device JSON, and clinical notes,

00:00:39.697 --> 00:00:44.272
this habit makes code reviews much easier because you can explain what the query is supposed to guarantee

00:00:44.272 --> 00:00:46.842
before discussing syntax.

00:00:46.842 --> 00:00:52.320
After running it, inspect a few records manually and check that the result matches that explanation.
